ae36437fff5b4fb5","event_uuid":"3d56dc90-a068-4fe6-a743-27e6b2dc5561","position":{"commit_sha":"4e966eecabb7f655ac9af939c63b7edb2a5c93cf","position":"1789015345811849001-3d56dc90-a068-4fe6-a743-27e6b2dc5561"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"81eb9a2c2c4295498bcda7a5256c2189485c415bafb03a70c137f0bf14ffa1ca","event_uuid":"79b8b2f1-66cc-41ba-adcc-e582825b5b59","position":{"commit_sha":"7542c60349df477427b6a0906ab5921b19548c7b","position":"1789015364490855001-79b8b2f1-66cc-41ba-adcc-e582825b5b59"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"flaky","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"RCA observation: Gerrit 2942 / GitHub run 34413282211 failed only tests/unit/test_marker_fcntl_guard.py::test_marker_lock_serializes_posix_access on ubuntu py3.11. Expected ['first-has-lock','first-done','second-done']; actual ['first-has-lock','second-done','first-done']. Current local macOS run of that test passes, so the failure is platform-dependent, not caused by the snapshot_alpha patch.","timestamp":1788996155655848001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"RCA hypothesis/confirmation: the test uses threads to model contention, but POSIX flock semantics are process-associated/platform-dependent for same-process descriptors. On Linux the second thread can take the marker lock while the first thread still holds its critical section, so the test oracle permits second-done before first-done. A control probe using separate processes preserves the intended cross-process serialization (before release only first-has-lock; after release first-done then second-done). Root cause is the test harness using same-process threads for a process-level lock contract; production cross-process locking remains correct.","timestamp":1788996179554947001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implementation evidence: replaced the same-process threaded contention oracle with a separate-process POSIX fcntl contention test using explicit inter-process events/pipe. Focused verification passed repeatedly: initial fixed run 3 passed; repeat command ran the module twice with both runs green; spawn context removed fork-in-multithread deprecation. make lint passed. Full make verify with PYTEST_WORKERS=2 progressed through lint/typecheck but the local host again stalled in unrelated long xdist execution; CI will provide the required full-suite verdict.","timestamp":1789002756315134001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Completion evidence for [non-codebase] verify criterion: the post-fix Gerrit run for change 2946 patchset 1, GitHub Actions run 34424792080, completed success. The failed run that discovered the issue on change 2942 was independently classified as this preexisting flaky marker-lock test oracle; after this ticket's fix landed, the same gating suite passed. Focused local evidence also passed: pytest tests/unit/test_marker_fcntl_guard.py -q passed three times, and make lint passed.","timestamp":1789006758212039001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Follow-up correction landed via Gerrit 2954, merged as 5c699979ae562. It drops the residual post-release global-order assertion and keeps the oracle focused on the lock-held invariant; CI run 34435159719 completed success with Verified +1.","timestamp":1789014701434967001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1788946659077839001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"eebc5f6e-1f83-4bed-a1c5-df6797541a7b","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"c437-d221-8471-47a7"},{"link_uuid":"6be4b0f0-84bb-4396-b02e-d2016444521f","relation":"blocks","target_id":"3e32-a859-2153-4a1b"},{"link_uuid":"2a9a58fc-e072-4fad-8f10-f08fa1a9fc6b","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"2a3d-aedc-7486-4052"},{"link_uuid":"51f87dd5-5781-4c4a-8e52-d7e806b127bc","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"4521-2aee-840c-44ba"},{"link_uuid":"912e19aa-652b-48ef-8e46-4a30be111fc3","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"33b8-a947-e995-4292"}],"description":"## Symptom\nGerrit change 2888 patch set 1 (359e5b214f99e8a43ffa2c9203fbd4a6aaf97cdc) received Verified -1 in GitHub Actions run 34326885726, job 102386780456, Python 3.12 default suite. Gerrit change 2942 later reproduced the same failure on ubuntu py3.11. Exactly one test failed while the rest of the suite passed:\n\n`tests/unit/test_marker_fcntl_guard.py::test_marker_lock_serializes_posix_access`\n\nExpected event order: `first-has-lock`, `first-done`, `second-done`. Actual order: `first-has-lock`, `second-done`, `first-done`.\n\n## Corrected scope boundary\nThis ticket owns the diagnosis and the test-harness fix. It does not change production marker-lock semantics unless RCA proves production locking is wrong. The current evidence points to a test oracle bug: `tests/unit/test_marker_fcntl_guard.py` uses `threading.Thread` inside one Python process to test a POSIX `flock` critical section, even though the real contract is process-level store/marker serialization.\n\n## Investigation plan\n- Reproduce or cite a CI reproduction of the exact ordering failure.\n- Compare current threaded test behavior with a separate-process contention probe against `rebar.reducer.marker.write_marker` / `remove_marker`.\n- Confirm whether production cross-process locking or the same-process threaded oracle is wrong.\n- Add a RED regression by changing the test to assert the real cross-process lock boundary; it should fail on the old thread-based oracle/platform model and pass once the oracle uses independent processes.\n- Implement the smallest test-only fix if production locking is confirmed correct.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] CI or a controlled failpoint documents the failing order `first-has-lock`, `second-done`, `first-done` from the old threaded oracle.\n- [x] RCA records that the existing test uses same-process `threading.Thread`, not a second process, and whether that matches the production contract.\n- [x] The fixed test exercises two independent processes contending on the marker lock file.\n- [x] The fixed test does not rely on `time.sleep` as the serialization oracle; it asserts only that the contender cannot complete while the holder is inside the locked critical section, then accepts either post-release completion order.\n- [x] Marker no-primitive fallback tests continue to pass.\n- [x] `pytest tests/unit/test_marker_fcntl_guard.py -q` passes repeatedly.\n- [x] [non-codebase] `make verify PYTEST_WORKERS=2` passes, or any failure is independently classified and not caused by this fix.\n  provenance: environment=GitHub Actions run 34424792080; principal=rebar CI bot; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — Gerrit Verified run for change 2946 patchset 1 completed success after this fix landed.","detected_by":"verified","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/unit/test_marker_fcntl_guard.py","reason":"Replace same-process thread contention oracle with process-level marker lock contention coverage."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["blocks","3e32-a859-2153-4a1b"],["relates_to","2a3d-aedc-7486-4052"],["relates_to","33b8-a947-e995-4292"],["relates_to","4521-2aee-840c-44ba"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"3d56dc90-a068-4fe6-a743-27e6b2dc5561","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":["ci","flaky-test","gerrit","locking"],"ticket_id":"f28d-cc1b-c3e3-45af","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Fix threaded marker lock oracle","verify_commands":[{"command":"pytest tests/unit/test_marker_fcntl_guard.py -q","dd_id":"AC1","dd_text":"marker lock contention regression"},{"command":"make verify PYTEST_WORKERS=2","dd_id":"AC2","dd_text":"full repository verification"}]},"source_event_uuids":["8a61c28e-6865-44b7-844c-ea820600c646","6124dc20-a410-4b27-a2d1-0509775e8fef","eb375126-7ad6-4105-8bcc-e52e85625c9c","acc262a9-b77a-4c29-9dbf-31c0bbfda35e","a9ede835-9fab-4bf4-89e3-455068141f8d","ce37a9d7-085f-461e-bff5-5af50851e256","f4f4773b-9ac9-4e20-8786-2fb31e11f7b4","3f79875f-33f2-4ffc-949f-db4a0fb09f55","bf8e5f10-ae44-427a-a123-9b2852f5e5c2","2a9a58fc-e072-4fad-8f10-f08fa1a9fc6b","aff4a1ad-1193-4886-a719-1451de627bdd","51f87dd5-5781-4c4a-8e52-d7e806b127bc","45ed5f38-9595-4cb1-91e6-e0a685a59c2b","9efcce43-7098-4b6b-acfa-385c8a93a9e1","4a6812f3-0517-4b1c-ba00-52573381f0b1","20b7ea5a-8f4b-4b3c-b1b2-2d0c7771e6b6","b365e837-a4e0-4618-a5fd-be0a8bc3749e","912e19aa-652b-48ef-8e46-4a30be111fc3","d3290559-b552-4d90-9bbc-ece66c7ea02c","3d56dc90-a068-4fe6-a743-27e6b2dc5561","79b8b2f1-66cc-41ba-adcc-e582825b5b59"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1789021393178852951,"uuid":"aaea06d3-6989-4932-8b50-c94088bac6dc"}